      "message": "No, you\u0027re right. As I flagged in the other comment, this was a quick hack to get it to work and doesn\u0027t pretend to be a C-compliant implementation. The (unique) call to the function is [here](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/dtc/+/0cdd06c5135bd9f46853c2f58ad2ac91b0fa87f3/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c#455):\n```\nindex \u003d strtoul(sep + 1, \u0026endptr, 10);\nif ((*endptr !\u003d \u0027\\0\u0027) || (endptr \u003c\u003d (sep + 1)))\n    return -FDT_ERR_BADOVERLAY;\n```\n\nso `base` is always `10`, `errno` is never used and the input string is the [`\u003coffset\u003e` of `__fixups__` entries](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/dtc/+/refs/heads/master/Documentation/dt-object-internal.txt#231), which is a positive offset (no sign, no prefix, always positive).\n\nI like the idea of re-using a proper C-compliant implementation. But we can\u0027t link against Bionic directly; I\u0027ll try to see how much I need to carve out of the library to do so.",
